        card("Culture note: the Katarungang Pambarangay", "The barangays are the smallest political subdivisions in the Philippines. The Katarungang Pambarangay (KP) or Barangay Justice System (BJS) is an alternative, community-based mechanism for dispute resolution of conflicts between members of the same community. The BJS provides a venue for disputing parties to search for a mutually acceptable solution. Other members of the communities act as intermediaries, facilitating the discussion of possible solutions. The BJS formalized the Filipino tradition to seek help of community elders or tribe leaders in resolving disputes between members of the same community, and uses the Punong Barangay (highest elected official in a barangay) and the Lupon members (committee of respected community members). It is only when the BJS has failed to resolve the dispute that the parties are allowed to bring their case to court. (gov.ph)"),
